INDEX_MD = """\
**Where is anything, and what is it related to?** `ce.index` answers both, over the CONTENT
of every app on the mesh at once - documents, pages, files, blocks, and the capabilities
themselves - plus a graph of typed relations across all of them.

Service discovery already answered *"what can this mesh do"*. This answers **"what does
this mesh know"**, which nothing did: every corpus had its own differently-shaped search, so
finding something meant already knowing which app owned it. And nothing anywhere computed or
stored a *relation* - two documents about the same problem, in two apps, were strangers
unless a human had typed a link.

## The three apps

| third | repo | owns |
|---|---|---|
| state | `ce-index-state` | items, typed edges, crawl cursors. Bounded per origin. No meaning. |
| logic | `ce-index` | every opinion: crawler, ranking, relations, the query API. No state. |
| viz | `ce-index-web` | the search box and the relation graph. |

Everything stored is **derived and rebuildable**. The index is a cache of what the mesh
answered, never a system of record: losing all of it costs one re-crawl and nothing else.

## Making your app searchable

Answer ONE op, `items`, on your own ctl topic. That is the entire integration - nothing is
registered anywhere and no reader for your app exists in the index. The crawler finds you
through the `node.facts` census and your own `describe`, so installing your app on any
machine puts its content in the index with zero configuration.

```
{"op": "items", "args": {"since": <unix>, "cursor": <opaque>, "limit": <int>}}
  -> {"items": [{id, kind, title, text, ref, updated, tags, links, meta}], "cursor", "more"}
```

## Start here

```
ce app install ./ce-index-state
ce app install ./ce-index
indexctl.py search per-origin quota
indexctl.py suggest draft.md          # where does this passage belong?
```

## The op this exists for

`suggest {text}` takes the passage you are **writing right now** - which lives in no app yet
- and answers where it belongs, what it duplicates, what is relevant to it, and which
existing things it should link to. The writer never has to already know the corpus.

## Can AI reach it

Yes, on every surface, with parity - an agent searches through the same ops, under the same
capability gates, as a human.

- **SDK** - `sdk/py/ceindex.py`, `sdk/js/ceindex.js`
- **API** - service `ce.index`, JSON on `index/ctl`, events on `index/events`
- **Capabilities** - `index:read` / `index:write`, defined in the app's own
  `cecapabilities.toml`
- **MCP** - `claude mcp add ce-index -- python3 clients/mcp/ce_index_mcp.py`
- **CLI** - `indexctl.py`
- **Cells** - `<ce-index-search>`, `<ce-index-graph>`

## The pages

1. [Why a search engine, and why a graph](#) - what each corpus could and could not do
   before this, and why the graph is the half that matters more.
2. [How it works](#) - census, crawl, rank, relate; the watermark, and what one cycle costs.
3. [The relation graph](#) - every relation type, why each edge explains itself, and the
   bounds that stop a shared tag exploding into an edge storm.
4. [The corpus contract](#) - the one op, what each optional field buys you, and the three
   modes an app can appear in.
5. [Operating the index](#) - install, knobs, reading `sources` honestly, what to do when a
   corpus indexes zero items, and the traps that cost live debugging rounds.

## Related work

- [[2026-07-26 · a distributed mesh-wide recursive search engine; similarity and relation graph over everything]] - the directive
- [[Build ce-index: the mesh-wide content search engine + typed relation graph (ce.index trio)]] - the work item and what shipped
- [[Sentinel - suspicious-activity flagging on the mesh]] - the sibling system that watches the substrate underneath
- [[App anatomy — State / Logic / Viz, docs, robustness]] - why this is three apps

## The one thing to remember

**Unknown is not empty.** A corpus that could not be reached, refused the crawler, or timed
out is reported as exactly that - never as a corpus that holds nothing. Every bound the
system applies (items per corpus, relation budget, text truncation) is reported too, because
a silent cap reads as "we indexed everything" when it did not.
"""


class Ocean:
    def __init__(self):
        self.client = ce.connect()
        found = self.client.find_service(SERVICE)
        if not found:
            raise SystemExit("ce.ocean is not on this mesh (install ocean-state + ocean)")
        self.provider = found[0]

    def call(self, op, args=None, timeout_ms=120000):
        raw = self.client.request(self.provider, CTL,
                                  json.dumps({"op": op, "args": args or {}}),
                                  timeout_ms=timeout_ms)
        reply = json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8") or "{}")
        if "error" in reply:
            raise RuntimeError(f"{op}: {reply['error']}")
        return reply.get("result")

    def org(self):
        for o in self.call("org.list")["orgs"]:
            if o.get("title") == ORG_NAME or o.get("name") == ORG_NAME:
                return o["id"]
        return self.call("org.create", {"name": ORG_NAME})["id"]

    def project(self, org):
        for p in self.call("project.list", {"org": org})["projects"]:
            if p.get("title") == PROJECT_NAME or p.get("name") == PROJECT_NAME:
                return p["id"]
        return self.call("project.create",
                         {"org": org, "name": PROJECT_NAME, "visibility": "open"})["id"]

    def upsert(self, title, md, project=None, parent=None, icon=None):
        """Create the doc, or update it in place if one with this title already exists here."""
        where = {"project": project} if project else {"parent": parent}
        existing = None
        try:
            for d in self.call("doc.list", where)["docs"]:
                if d.get("title") == title:
                    existing = d["id"]
                    break
        except RuntimeError:
            pass
        if existing:
            self.call("doc.update", {"doc": existing, "title": title, "md": md,
                                     **({"icon": icon} if icon else {})})
            return existing, "updated"
        args = {"title": title, "md": md, **where}
        if icon:
            args["icon"] = icon
        return self.call("doc.create", args)["id"], "created"


def workspace_titles(o):
    """Every document title the caller can see -> id. `graph` is the one op that answers
    across the whole workspace, so it is what a link check should be built on."""
    titles = {}
    for node in o.call("graph").get("nodes") or ():
        if node.get("kind") == "doc" and node.get("title"):
            titles.setdefault(str(node["title"]).strip(), node["id"])
    return titles


def related_block(fname, titles):
    """A `## Related` section of VERIFIED wiki links, plus whatever could not be found."""
    entries = RELATED.get(fname) or []
    if not entries:
        return "", []
    live, missing = [], []
    for title, why in entries:
        if title in titles:
            live.append(f"- [[{title}]] - {why}")
        else:
            missing.append(title)
    if not live:
        return "", missing
    return "\n\n## Related\n\n" + "\n".join(live) + "\n", missing


def title_and_body(path):
    """The first `# ` heading is the document title; the rest is the body."""
    text = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read()
    lines = text.split("\n")
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        if line.startswith("# "):
            return line[2:].strip(), "\n".join(lines[i + 1:]).strip("\n")
    return os.path.basename(path), text


def main():
    dry = "--dry-run" in sys.argv
    missing = [f for f, _ in PAGES if not os.path.exists(os.path.join(DOCS, f))]
    if missing:
        raise SystemExit(f"missing doc source: {', '.join(missing)}")

    if dry:
        print(f"would publish into Ocean: org {ORG_NAME} / project {PROJECT_NAME}")
        print(f"  {INDEX_TITLE}")
        for fname, icon in PAGES:
            title, body = title_and_body(os.path.join(DOCS, fname))
            print(f"    {title}  ({len(body)} bytes)")
        return 0

    o = Ocean()
    org = o.org()
    project = o.project(org)
    print(f"org {org[:12]} / project {project[:12]}")

    index_id, how = o.upsert(INDEX_TITLE, INDEX_MD, project=project, icon="mag")
    print(f"  {how:8} {INDEX_TITLE}")

    titles = workspace_titles(o)
    unresolved = []
    for fname, icon in PAGES:
        title, body = title_and_body(os.path.join(DOCS, fname))
        block, missing = related_block(fname, titles)
        unresolved += [(fname, m) for m in missing]
        _, how = o.upsert(title, body + block, parent=index_id, icon=icon)
        links = block.count("[[")
        print(f"  {how:8} {title}" + (f"   (+{links} links)" if links else ""))

    if unresolved:
        # Never silent: an unwritten link is a link someone expected to see.
        print("\nNOT LINKED — no document with these titles exists:")
        for fname, title in unresolved:
            print(f"  {fname}: {title[:78]}")

    print(f"\nread it: ocean/oceanctl.py md {index_id}")
    print("re-run this after editing ce-index/docs/*.md — it updates in place")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
